+## 1. Headline: the anti-duplicate guard has NO issue-existence validation (source-level)
+
+Read `.github/workflows/pipeline.yml` on main (inline job `duplicate-pr-guard`, "Verify no competing open PR exists for the same issue"). Mechanism as coded:
+
+1. Target extraction: explicit `(closes|fixes|resolves) #N` in title/body -> else branch `issue-N` tokens -> else **fallback: ANY `#N` token** in title/body (`grep -oE '#[0-9]+' | sort -u`).
+2. Cross-PR match: for each extracted token, scans OTHER open PRs (`gh pr list --state open --json number,title,body,headRefName`) for a closing-statement on the same token **OR a bare digit token in the branch name** (`(^|[^0-9])N([^0-9]|$)`).
+3. On match: `::error::Competing PR detected! Another open PR already targets #N.` exit 1.
+
+Findings that sharpen #2854's Class A:
+- **No existence check anywhere**: a cited token is treated as a hard target whether or not the issue exists. Two PRs sharing any bogus token (e.g. #999999) mutually exclude — exactly the 3/4-runs identical signature (#2848/#2847/#2840: "Another open PR already targets #999999").
+- **The fallback is the widening**: with no explicit closing statement, ANY #N mention (e.g. a work-order citation or template placeholder in the body) becomes a claimed target. #999999 literal is ABSENT from pipeline.yml -> the sentinel is data-borne, riding PR bodies/branches. This confirms #2854's "defect is upstream" at source level and makes its admin recommendation (c) — validate cited issue existence before the guard runs — source-confirmed necessary, not optional.
+- **Escape hatch exists**: a `guard-exempt` label skips the guard entirely (`PR_LABELS` check, first line of the job) — relevant for admin remediation and for rescue lanes.
+
